{"text": "January", "etymologies": [{"etymologyHTML": "<p>From Middle English <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"enm\">Januarie</i>, <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"enm\">januari</i>, re-latinised forms of Middle English <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"enm\">Janevere</i>, <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"enm\">Ieneuer</i>, from Anglo-Norman <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"fro\">genever</i>, from Latin <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"la\">I\u0101nu\u0101rius</i> (\u201c(month) of Janus\u201d), a compound of <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"la\">I\u0101nus</i> (\"Janus\") +\u200e <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"la\">-\u0101rius</i> (adjectival suffix), with the first element perhaps from the Proto-Indo-European root <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"ine-pro\">*yeh\u2082-</i> (\u201cto go\u201d). Doublet of <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">Gennaro</i>.\n</p>", "pos": []}], "pronunciation": [["General Australian", "/\u02c8d\u0361\u0292\u00e6nj\u0289\u02cce\u02d0\u0279i/"], ["UK", "/\u02c8d\u0361\u0292\u00e6n.j(\u028a.)\u0259.\u0279i/"], ["obsolete", "/\u02c8d\u0361\u0292\u026an\u0259\u02ccw\u025b\u0259\u0279i/"], ["US", "/\u02c8d\u0361\u0292\u00e6nju\u02cc\u025b\u0279i/"]]}